text: ['Affinity for Forests (This spell costs {1} less to cast for each Forest you control.)', 'Affinity for Islands (This spell costs {1} less to cast for each Island you control.)\\nFlying', 'Affinity for Mountains (This spell costs {1} less to cast for each Mountain you control.)\\nHaste', 'Affinity for Plains (This spell costs {1} less to cast for each Plains you control.)\\nVigilance', "Affinity for Swamps (This spell costs {1} less to cast for each Swamp you control.)\\nFear (This creature can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.)", 'Affinity for artifacts (This spell costs {1} less to cast for each artifact you control.)\\nFlying\\nWhen Chromescale Drake enters the battlefield, reveal the top three cards of your library. Put all artifact cards revealed this way into your hand and the rest into your graveyard.', 'Affinity for artifacts (This spell costs {1} less to cast for each artifact you control.)\\nFlying\\nWhen Furnace Dragon enters the battlefield, if you cast it from your hand, exile all artifacts.', "Affinity for artifacts (This spell costs {1} less to cast for each artifact you control.)\\nWhen Quicksilver Behemoth attacks or blocks, return it to its owner's hand at end of combat. (Return it only if it's on the battlefield.)", 'All combat damage that would be dealt to you this turn is dealt to target attacking creature instead.', 'All creatures able to block equipped creature do so.\\nEquip {3} ({3}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery. This card enters the battlefield unattached and stays on the battlefield if the creature leaves.)', "All permanents are artifacts in addition to their other types.\\nAll cards that aren't on the battlefield, spells, and permanents are colorless.\\nPlayers may spend mana as though it were mana of any color.", 'Artifact creatures you control gain flying until end of turn.', 'Artifacts you control have indestructible. (Effects that say "destroy" don\'t destroy them. Artifact creatures with indestructible can\'t be destroyed by damage.)', 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice an artifact.\\nSearch your library for an artifact card with mana value X or less, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'As long as Auriok Glaivemaster is equipped, it gets +1/+1 and has first strike.', 'As long as Thunderstaff is untapped, if a creature would deal combat damage to you, prevent 1 of that damage.\\n{2}, {T}: Attacking creatures get +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'As long as Trinisphere is untapped, each spell that would cost less than three mana to cast costs three mana to cast. (Additional mana in the cost may be paid with any color of mana or colorless mana. For example, a spell that would cost {1}{B} to cast costs {2}{B} to cast instead.)', 'At the beginning of your end step, if Nim Abomination is untapped, you lose 3 life.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, put a +1/+1 counter on each creature with modular you control.\\nModular 6 (This creature enters the battlefield with six +1/+1 counters on it. When it dies, you may put its +1/+1 counters on target artifact creature.)', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice a permanent.\\nWhenever Greater Harvester deals combat damage to a player, that player sacrifices two permanents.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, you may put a charge counter on Aether Vial.\\n{T}: You may put a creature card with mana value equal to the number of charge counters on Aether Vial from your hand onto the battlefield.', 'Cast this spell only during the declare attackers step.\\nAttacking creatures you control get +X/+0 until end of turn, where X is the number of attacking creatures. Sacrifice those creatures at the beginning of the next end step.', 'Cast this spell only during your turn and only during combat.\\nChoose one —\\n• Creatures you control gain double strike until end of turn.\\n• Untap all creatures you control. After this phase, there is an additional combat phase.\\nEntwine {1}{R} (Choose both if you pay the entwine cost.)', 'Change the target of target spell with a single target.', 'Choose one —\\n• Barbed Lightning deals 3 damage to target creature.\\n• Barbed Lightning deals 3 damage to target player or planeswalker.\\nEntwine {2} (Choose both if you pay the entwine cost.)', 'Choose one —\\n• Creatures you control get +2/+2 until end of turn.\\n• Until end of turn, creatures you control gain "Whenever this creature deals damage, you gain that much life."\\nEntwine {1}{W} (Choose both if you pay the entwine cost.)', 'Choose one —\\n• Destroy target land.\\n• Search your library for a land card, put that card onto the battlefield, then shuffle.\\nEntwine {1}{G} (Choose both if you pay the entwine cost.)', "Choose one —\\n• Look at the top five cards of target opponent's library, then put them back in any order.\\n• Look at the top five cards of your library, then put them back in any order.\\nEntwine {U} (Choose both if you pay the entwine cost.)", "Choose one —\\n• Until end of turn, whenever a creature is dealt damage, destroy it.\\n• Until end of turn, whenever a creature dies, that creature's controller loses life equal to its toughness.\\nEntwine {2}{B} (Choose both if you pay the entwine cost.)", "Counter target spell. That spell's controller may draw a card.", 'Crazed Goblin attacks each combat if able.', "Create a 3/3 green Beast creature token. Then if an opponent controls more creatures than you, return Pulse of the Tangle to its owner's hand.", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nProtection from artifacts\\nWhenever an opponent casts an artifact spell, you may create a 1/1 green Insect creature token.", 'Destroy all nonartifact permanents.', 'Destroy target Equipment. If that Equipment was attached to a creature, Unforge deals 2 damage to that creature.', 'Destroy target artifact and all other artifacts with the same name as that artifact.', "Destroy target artifact creature or black creature. It can't be regenerated.", 'Destroy target artifact. If that artifact had counters on it, put that many +1/+1 counters or charge counters on an artifact you control.', "Destroy target artifact. It can't be regenerated.", 'Destroy target enchantment and all other enchantments with the same name as that enchantment.', "Destroy target nonblack creature. It can't be regenerated. You gain control of all Equipment that were attached to it. (This effect lasts indefinitely.)", "Draw two cards, then discard a card. Then if an opponent has more cards in hand than you, return Pulse of the Grid to its owner's hand.", "Each creature you control can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an artifact land.", 'Each player loses X life, discards X cards, sacrifices X creatures, then sacrifices X lands.', 'Enchant Equipment\\nWhen Carry Away enters the battlefield, unattach enchanted Equipment.\\nYou control enchanted Equipment.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets -1/-1.\\nWhen enchanted creature dies, return Screams from Within from your graveyard to the battlefield.', 'Enchant permanent\\nWhen Psychic Overload enters the battlefield, tap enchanted permanent.\\nEnchanted permanent doesn\'t untap during its controller\'s untap step.\\nEnchanted permanent has "Discard two artifact cards: Untap this permanent."', 'Equipment named Sword of Kaldra, Shield of Kaldra, and Helm of Kaldra have indestructible.\\nEquipped creature has indestructible. (Damage and effects that say "destroy" don\'t destroy it.)\\nEquip {4}', "Equipped creature can't be blocked and has shroud. (It can't be the target of spells or abilities.)\\nEquip {2}", 'Equipped creature gets +1/+0.\\nWhenever equipped creature deals combat damage to a player, that player discards a card.\\nEquip {1} ({1}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery. This card enters the battlefield unattached and stays on the battlefield if the creature leaves.)', 'Equipped creature gets +1/-1.\\nWhenever equipped creature dies, draw two cards.\\nEquip {1}', 'Equipped creature gets +2/+1 and has "{T}, Unattach Heartseeker: Destroy target creature."\\nEquip {5} ({5}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery. This card enters the battlefield unattached and stays on the battlefield if the creature leaves.)', 'Equipped creature gets +2/+2 and has protection from red and from blue.\\nWhenever equipped creature deals combat damage to a player, Sword of Fire and Ice deals 2 damage to any target and you draw a card.\\nEquip {2}', 'Equipped creature gets +2/+2 and has protection from white and from black.\\nWhenever equipped creature deals combat damage to a player, you gain 3 life and you may return up to one target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.\\nEquip {2}', 'Equipped creature gets +2/+2.\\nEquip {2} ({2}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', 'Equipped creature has "{T}, Unattach Leonin Bola: Tap target creature."\\nEquip {1} ({1}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery. This card enters the battlefield unattached and stays on the battlefield if the creature leaves.)', 'Equipped creature has first strike and "{T}, Unattach Surestrike Trident: This creature deals damage equal to its power to target player or planeswalker."\\nEquip {4} ({4}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery. This card enters the battlefield unattached and stays on the battlefield if the creature leaves.)', 'Essence Drain deals 3 damage to any target and you gain 3 life.', "Fear (This creature can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.)\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you may move a +1/+1 counter from target creature onto Arcbound Fiend.\\nModular 3 (This creature enters the battlefield with three +1/+1 counters on it. When it dies, you may put its +1/+1 counters on target artifact creature.)", 'First strike\\nModular 4 (This creature enters the battlefield with four +1/+1 counters on it. When it dies, you may put its +1/+1 counters on target artifact creature.)', "Flamebreak deals 3 damage to each creature without flying and each player. Creatures dealt damage this way can't be regenerated this turn.", 'Flash (You may cast this spell any time you could cast an instant.)\\nReach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)', 'Flying, trample\\nWhen Eater of Days enters the battlefield, you skip your next two turns.', 'Flying\\nAs long as Pristine Angel is untapped, it has protection from artifacts and from all colors.\\nWhenever you cast a spell, you may untap Pristine Angel.', "Flying\\nDiscard an artifact card: Return Neurok Prodigy to its owner's hand.", "Flying\\nDrill-Skimmer has shroud as long as you control another artifact creature. (It can't be the target of spells or abilities.)", 'Flying\\nHoverguard Observer can block only creatures with flying.', 'Flying\\nIndestructible (Damage and effects that say "destroy" don\'t destroy this creature.)', 'Flying\\nModular 1 (This creature enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it. When it dies, you may put its +1/+1 counters on target artifact creature.)', 'Flying\\nSacrifice Pteron Ghost: Regenerate target artifact.', 'Flying\\nWhenever Emissary of Despair deals combat damage to a player, that player loses 1 life for each artifact they control.', 'Flying\\nWhenever Emissary of Hope deals combat damage to a player, you gain 1 life for each artifact that player controls.', 'Flying\\n{B}, Pay 1 life: Grimclaw Bats gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Haste\\nModular 2 (This creature enters the battlefield with two +1/+1 counters on it. When it dies, you may put its +1/+1 counters on target artifact creature.)', 'Imprint — When Spellbinder enters the battlefield, you may exile an instant card from your hand.\\nWhenever equipped creature deals combat damage to a player, you may copy the exiled card. If you do, you may cast the copy without paying its mana cost.\\nEquip {4}', 'Imprint — {1}: Exile target creature card from your graveyard.\\nAs long as a card exiled with Death-Mask Duplicant has flying, Death-Mask Duplicant has flying. The same is true for fear, first strike, double strike, haste, landwalk, protection, and trample.', 'Imprint — {X}, {T}: You may exile an instant or sorcery card with mana value X from your hand.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you may copy a card exiled with Panoptic Mirror. If you do, you may cast the copy without paying its mana cost.', 'Indestructible (Damage and effects that say "destroy" don\'t destroy this artifact.)\\n{3}: Darksteel Brute becomes a 2/2 Beast artifact creature until end of turn.', 'Indestructible (Effects that say "destroy" don\'t destroy this artifact.)\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you may put a charge counter on Darksteel Reactor.\\nWhen Darksteel Reactor has twenty or more charge counters on it, you win the game.', 'Indestructible (Effects that say "destroy" don\'t destroy this artifact.)\\nMyr creatures get +1/+1.\\n{5}: Create a 1/1 colorless Myr artifact creature token.', 'Indestructible (Effects that say "destroy" don\'t destroy this artifact.)\\n{1}, {T}: Scry 1. (Look at the top card of your library. You may put that card on the bottom of your library.)', 'Indestructible (Effects that say "destroy" don\'t destroy this artifact.)\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color.', 'Indestructible\\n{T}: Add {C}.', 'Inflame deals 2 damage to each creature dealt damage this turn.', "Juggernaut attacks each combat if able.\\nJuggernaut can't be blocked by Walls.", 'Karstoderm enters the battlefield with five +1/+1 counters on it.\\nWhenever an artifact enters the battlefield, remove a +1/+1 counter from Karstoderm.', 'Look at the top X cards of your library, where X is the number of artifacts you control. Put one of those cards into your hand and the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.', "Mephitic Ooze gets +1/+0 for each artifact you control.\\nWhenever Mephitic Ooze deals combat damage to a creature, destroy that creature. The creature can't be regenerated.", 'Modular 1 (This creature enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it. When it dies, you may put its +1/+1 counters on target artifact creature.)', 'Modular 3 (This creature enters the battlefield with three +1/+1 counters on it. When it dies, you may put its +1/+1 counters on target artifact creature.)', 'Prevent all damage target spell would deal this turn. You gain life equal to the damage prevented this way.', 'Prevent the next 3 damage that would be dealt to target creature this turn. For each 1 damage prevented this way, put a +1/+1 counter on that creature.', 'Protection from artifacts', "Pulse of the Forge deals 4 damage to target player or planeswalker. Then if that player or that planeswalker's controller has more life than you, return Pulse of the Forge to its owner's hand.", 'Put two +1/+1 counters on target creature and two +1/+1 counters on another target creature.', "Put two target artifacts on top of their owners' libraries.", 'Remove a +1/+1 counter from Arcbound Reclaimer: Put target artifact card from your graveyard on top of your library.\\nModular 2 (This creature enters the battlefield with two +1/+1 counters on it. When it dies, you may put its +1/+1 counters on target artifact creature.)', 'Remove all counters from all permanents and exile all tokens.', "Return all artifacts you control to their owner's hand.", 'Return target artifact card from your graveyard to your hand.', "Return target nonland permanent and all other permanents with the same name as that permanent to their owners' hands.", 'Sacrifice a creature: Put a charge counter on Spawning Pit.\\n{1}, Remove two charge counters from Spawning Pit: Create a 2/2 colorless Spawn artifact creature token.', 'Sacrifice an artifact: Put a +1/+1 counter on Arcbound Ravager.\\nModular 1 (This creature enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it. When it dies, you may put its +1/+1 counters on target artifact creature.)', 'Sacrifice an artifact: Target artifact gains indestructible until end of turn.', "Scavenging Scarab can't block.", 'Tap all artifacts.', 'Target creature and all other creatures with the same name as that creature get +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Target creature and all other creatures with the same name as that creature get -2/-2 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn for each artifact you control.', 'Target opponent chooses an artifact card in their graveyard. Put that card onto the battlefield under your control.', 'Target player loses 1 life for each tapped artifact they control.', "Target player reveals three cards from their hand and you choose one of them. That player discards that card. Then if that player has more cards in hand than you, return Pulse of the Dross to its owner's hand.", "This spell can't be countered.\\nCounter target spell.", 'This spell costs {1} more to cast for each target beyond the first.\\nFireball deals X damage divided evenly, rounded down, among any number of targets.', "Trample, indestructible\\nIf Darksteel Colossus would be put into a graveyard from anywhere, reveal Darksteel Colossus and shuffle it into its owner's library instead.", 'Trample\\nWhenever another artifact enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on Arcbound Crusher.\\nModular 1 (This creature enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it. When it dies, you may put its +1/+1 counters on target artifact creature.)', 'When Chittering Rats enters the battlefield, target opponent puts a card from their hand on top of their library.', 'When Myr Moonvessel dies, add {C}.', 'When Sundering Titan enters or leaves the battlefield, choose a land of each basic land type, then destroy those lands.', 'When Vulshok War Boar enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you sacrifice an artifact.', 'Whenever Arcbound Slith deals combat damage to a player, put a +1/+1 counter on it.\\nModular 1 (This creature enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it. When it dies, you may put its +1/+1 counters on target artifact creature.)', 'Whenever Fangren Firstborn attacks, put a +1/+1 counter on each attacking creature.', "Whenever Gemini Engine attacks, create a colorless Construct artifact creature token named Twin that's attacking. Its power is equal to Gemini Engine's power and its toughness is equal to Gemini Engine's toughness. Sacrifice the token at end of combat.", 'Whenever Roaring Slagwurm attacks, tap all artifacts.', "Whenever Spincrusher blocks, put a +1/+1 counter on it.\\nRemove a +1/+1 counter from Spincrusher: Spincrusher can't be blocked this turn.", 'Whenever Tel-Jilad Wolf becomes blocked by an artifact creature, Tel-Jilad Wolf gets +3/+3 until end of turn.', "Whenever a nontoken creature enters the battlefield, if Genesis Chamber is untapped, that creature's controller creates a 1/1 colorless Myr artifact creature token.", 'Whenever a player casts a black spell, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts a blue spell, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts a green spell, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts a red spell, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts a white spell, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts an artifact spell, that player gains control of Drooling Ogre. (This effect lasts indefinitely.)', 'Whenever a source you control other than Talon of Pain deals damage to an opponent, put a charge counter on Talon of Pain.\\n{X}, {T}, Remove X charge counters from Talon of Pain: It deals X damage to any target.', 'Whenever an opponent casts a nonartifact spell, put a charge counter on Chimeric Egg.\\nRemove three charge counters from Chimeric Egg: Chimeric Egg becomes a 6/6 Construct artifact creature with trample until end of turn.', 'Whenever an opponent discards a card, you may draw a card.', 'Whenever you gain life, put that many +1/+1 counters on Ageless Entity.', 'Whenever you gain life, you may pay {X}, where X is less than or equal to the amount of life you gained. If you do, draw X cards.', "You don't lose the game for having 0 or less life.\\nWhenever you lose life, sacrifice a permanent for each 1 life you lost. (Damage causes loss of life.)", "You gain 4 life. Then if an opponent has more life than you, return Pulse of the Fields to its owner's hand.", 'You gain 6 life.', 'You may activate equip abilities any time you could cast an instant.', '{1}, {T}: Add one mana of any color.', "{1}: Target artifact creature blocks Auriok Siege Sled this turn if able.\\n{1}: Target artifact creature can't block Auriok Siege Sled this turn.", '{1}{G}, Sacrifice Viridian Zealot: Destroy target artifact or enchantment.', '{1}{U}{U}: Target permanent becomes an artifact in addition to its other types. (This effect lasts indefinitely.)\\n{3}{U}: Gain control of target artifact. (This effect lasts indefinitely.)', '{2}, {T}, Sacrifice a land: Draw a card and put a charge counter on Arcane Spyglass.\\nRemove three charge counters from Arcane Spyglass: Draw a card.', '{2}: Untap target artifact creature.', '{3}, {T}: Flip a coin. If you win the flip, create a 2/2 colorless Insect artifact creature token with flying named Wirefly. If you lose the flip, destroy all permanents named Wirefly.', '{R}, {T}: Flip a coin. If you win the flip, destroy target artifact and untap Goblin Archaeologist. If you lose the flip, sacrifice Goblin Archaeologist.', '{T}, Sacrifice an Island: Create a 2/2 blue Elemental creature token with flying.\\n{T}, Sacrifice a Mountain: Create a 3/3 red Elemental creature token.', '{T}, Sacrifice an artifact: Add {R}{R}.', '{T}: Add two mana of any one color. Spend this mana only to cast artifact spells or activate abilities of artifacts.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\nAny time you could mulligan and Serum Powder is in your hand, you may exile all the cards from your hand, then draw that many cards. (You can do this in addition to taking mulligans.)', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}: Blinkmoth Nexus becomes a 1/1 Blinkmoth artifact creature with flying until end of turn. It's still a land.\\n{1}, {T}: Target Blinkmoth creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.", "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Put a charge counter on Mirrodin's Core.\\n{T}, Remove a charge counter from Mirrodin's Core: Add one mana of any color.", '{T}: Add {C}{C}.', '{T}: Put a charge counter on target artifact.\\nSacrifice Coretapper: Put two charge counters on target artifact.', '{T}: Target creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.\\nWhenever you cast a spell, you may untap Leonin Battlemage.', '{T}: Target land becomes an artifact in addition to its other types until end of turn.', "{U}: Target creature becomes an artifact in addition to its other types until end of turn.\\n{U}: Until end of turn, target artifact creature becomes blue and isn't an artifact.", "{W}, {T}, Return Steelshaper Apprentice to its owner's hand: Search your library for an Equipment card, reveal that card, put it into your hand, then shuffle.", '{W}, {T}: Tap target creature.', '{X}, {T}: Tap X target noncreature artifacts.\\n{X}, {T}: Untap X target noncreature artifacts.', "{X}, {T}: Target opponent reveals cards from the top of their library until an artifact card or X cards are revealed, whichever comes first. If an artifact card is revealed this way, put it onto the battlefield under your control and sacrifice Thought Dissector. Put the rest of the revealed cards into that player's graveyard."]
flavor: ['"As the experimental population grows, so do the number of myr. It\'s a perfect equilibrium."\\n—Memnarch', '"Ashes to ashes, rust to rust."\\n—Viridian shaman', '"Bend with the storm, then reply in kind."', '"Did it have this shape upon Mirrodin\'s creation, or did some inconceivable force shape the unshapable?"\\n—Pontifex, elder researcher', '"Give me a bit of steel and I\'ll deliver it into the hearts of my enemies."', '"I have seen the end of times, a future in which all our kind are torn from this world."\\n—Ushanti, leonin shaman', '"I used to joke that he had been exiled for being too smart. Now I know why he never laughed."\\n—Glissa Sunseeker', '"I will fight only the way nature intended—and nature intended us to win."', '"If only the living were so easily salvaged."\\n—Memnarch', '"Is it the stomping kind or the munching kind?"\\n—Slobad, goblin tinkerer', '"May you wake to find you were only ever a dream."\\n—Mephidross curse', '"Now I\'m thirsty."\\n—Korva, Vulshok battlemaster', '"Secrets are meant to remain secret."\\n—Memnarch', '"Someday, someone will best me. But it won\'t be today, and it won\'t be you."', '"The druids would be better off if they spent more time in the lab and less time watching trees grow."\\n—Pontifex, elder researcher', '"The lifespan of a wirefly can be precisely described as \'short.\'"\\n—Bruenna, Neurok leader', '"The one who dies with the most toys is still dead."\\n—Geth, keeper of the Vault', '"Today\'s paperweight, tomorrow\'s leveler."\\n—Bruenna, Neurok leader', '"We have no sun to guide our dead, so I tend the prismatic flames of the spirit fires that show the souls their way. When I die, I hope there is one left to guide my spirit home."', '"When the levelers come again, we shall be ready for them."', '"Why should I be bound by rules when I can see so far beyond them?"', '"You might want to work on your aim."', '"Your arrogance is my best weapon."', 'A Vulshok weapon strikes with the fire of the forge that made it.', 'A single fear unleashes a torrent of nightmares.', 'A single lie unleashes a tide of disbelief.', 'A single light unleashes a hail of cleansing.', 'A single misstep unleashes an avalanche of ruin.', 'A single seed unleashes a flurry of growth.', 'A wurm knows nothing of deception. If it opens its mouth, it plans to eat you.', "After the researcher's astonishing success, his assistants spent six hours finding a way to return the specimens safely to the ground.", 'Always easily impressed, Durg was about to be blown away.', 'Art is unknown to the vedalken—for them, all creations must serve a purpose.', 'As long as there are questions to be asked, the vedalken will ask them.', 'As the nim storm across the plains, a lone priest stands in their path. At his silent gesture, the battle line breaks, and the tide turns.', 'Because fighting is easier than figuring out what else to do.', 'Before labs or lectures, there was insight.', 'Before predators or prey, there was life.', 'Before religion or civilization, there was order.', 'Before tyrants or torturers, there was evil.', 'Before wars or weapons, there was anger.', 'Bottom feeders sometimes rise to the top.', 'Break in case of emergency.', 'Bright as a mirror, dark as the sea.', 'Compared to the fire of the forge, the strength of steel is nothing.', "Defending to the death isn't always enough.", 'Even on a world of metal, there are those who thirst for blood.', 'Every creature on Mirrodin is a lightning rod.', 'Everything in its path is either pushed aside or ground under.', 'Fallen enemies are fed to the scavengers. Fallen friends are thrown into the Great Furnace, their souls returned to the Great Mother.', 'For the first and last time, the horrific creature experienced terror.', "From the Radix at the hub of the Tangle all the way out to the Edges of Forgetting, a Viridian elf's life is built around the temporary.", 'Gelfruit grows abundantly wherever Sylvok druids live, as if the Tangle knows that humans are not as hardy as the beasts or as nimble as the elves.', 'Her instinct is as sharp as her blade.', 'If taken, it cuts the hand that clutches it. If given, it heals the hand that holds it.', "In Mephidross, refuse doesn't last long—it's all scavenged, reanimated, or consumed.", 'In bringing life to Mirrodin, Memnarch was more successful than he knew—for Mirrodin began to take on a life of its own.', 'In close proximity, their magnetic energies merge and form a field of protection.', 'In the Tangle, bad is often followed by worse.', 'In the blur between metal and flesh, Memnarch found madness.', 'It breaches not physical distances but temporal ones.', "It converts the faintest surges of power from Mirrodin's core into usable energy, providing endless power for Memnarch's creations on the surface.", 'It could be made to run silently, but its low hum reminds the Neurok that they are always watched.', 'It gives legs to the earth and wings to the sky.', 'It is one of the oldest nim, steeped so long in the Dross that it has lost all vestiges of humanity.', 'It must eat its weight in metal daily, or its furnacelike belly will consume itself for lack of fuel.', 'It rolls with the punches.', 'It still stares accusingly at Memnarch, though millennia have passed since he separated the eye from its body.', 'Its curve mimics the twists of life and death.', "Leonin raising ceremonies take place at the white sun's dawn, the rebirth of artifacts mirroring the birth of a new day.", 'Memnarch created the myr with three qualities in mind: dependability, controllability, and disposability.', 'Memnarch shared a touch of his power with the vedalken in return for their service. It is a debt he intends to collect.', 'Mephidross claims all life within it. What cannot be twisted is absorbed.', "One thing the myr can't do is enjoy the scenery.", "Panopticon, forge of the Darksteel Eye, home of Mirrodin's keeper.", 'Scavengers are always the first to pay their respects.', "Some say the knowledge lost during the Ritual of Rebuking is returned through the well's waters.", 'Stealing goblin weapons would be easier if the goblins were smart enough to let go.', 'Strange times make for strange allies.', "Tel-Jilad's sworn protectors are the trolls, yet more fearsome protectors were created by the Tangle itself.", "Thanks to the wolves, Tel-Jilad is the one area of Mirrodin the myr don't see often.", 'The Auriok have fought the metal hordes for so long now that knowing how to cripple them has become an instinct.', 'The beetles feed not on the flesh of corpses but on the metal, grinding out the iron and steel to add to their own bulky shells.', "The book shrieks horribly until its cover is opened, granting the spirit inside a moment's rest from the painful stirrings of the book's contents.", 'The goblins built it far larger than the cave opening, but to their glee, it smashed into the mountainside, ripping itself a new exit.', 'The longer it patrols the smoldering crags of the Oxidda Chain, the more it adopts their fiery temper.', 'The longer it skulks through the corrosive gases of Mephidross, the more it adopts their thirst for death.', 'The longer it soars above the shimmering swirls of the Quicksilver Sea, the more it adopts their unpredictability.', 'The longer it stands among the deadly blades of the Razor Fields, the more it adopts their harsh exterior.', 'The longer it weaves through the twisted vines of the Tangle, the more it adopts their hidden strength.', 'The parts are as strong as the whole.', 'The spell fell upon the crowd like a dragon, ancient and full of death.', 'The strongest of the pride are measured not by the steel in their hands but by the steel in their souls.', "The swarm's million wings stir the foulest of breezes.", 'The ultimate treasure is one that guards itself.', 'The undead may outlast the living, but those who have never lived outlast them both.', "Their pain is so great, they can't help but share it with others.", 'Theirs is a craft brought about by necessity, now raised to the level of art.', "There's no escaping an enemy that lives inside your head.", "They're considered good luck by the elves they don't eat.", 'Those who survive the test bear a mark of power anyone can recognize.', 'Though no longer attached to the hand, it still holds its adversary in its grasp.', "When Mirrodin's varied civilizations developed ways to fight the levelers, Memnarch upped the stakes.", 'When leonin settlers abandon their homes to the nim, items of value are often left behind.', 'Wurms compete for nesting grounds near the Radix. The young who hatch closest have the best chance for survival.']
artist: ['Adam Rex', 'Alan Pollack', 'Alan Rabinowitz', 'Alex Horley-Orlandelli', 'Anthony S. Waters', 'Arnie Swekel', 'Ben Thompson', 'Brian Snõddy', 'Carl Critchlow', 'Christopher Moeller', 'D. Alexander Gregory', 'Dany Orizio', 'Daren Bader', 'Darrell Riche', 'Dave Dorman', 'David Martin', 'Donato Giancola', 'Edward P. Beard, Jr.', 'Glen Angus', 'Greg Hildebrandt', 'Greg Staples', 'Heather Hudson', 'Hugh Jamieson', 'Ittoku', 'Jeff Easley', 'Jeff Miracola', 'Jeremy Jarvis', 'Jim Murray', 'Jim Nelson', 'John Avon', 'John Matson', 'Jon Foster', 'Kaja Foglio', 'Kev Walker', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Luca Zontini', 'Mark Tedin', 'Mark Zug', 'Martina Pilcerova', 'Matt Cavotta', 'Matt Thompson', 'Matthew D. Wilson', 'Michael Sutfin', 'Nottsuo', 'Paolo Parente', 'Pete Venters', 'Puddnhead', 'Rob Alexander', 'Ron Spencer', 'Scott M. Fischer', 'Stephen Tappin', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Thomas M. Baxa', 'Tim Hildebrandt', 'Tom Wänerstrand', 'Tony Szczudlo', 'Trevor Hairsine', 'Vance Kovacs', 'Wayne England', 'rk post']
